# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values from your Supabase
# project (Project Settings > Data API, and Project Settings > API Keys).
# .env.local is ignored by Git, so your values stay on your computer.
#
# Both values are safe for the browser: the publishable key can only do what
# the database's security rules allow. NEVER put the secret key
# (sb_secret_...) in this file or in any NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your-key

# --- AI analysis (Phase 3, optional) ---
# Add ONE of these keys (if both are set, Claude is used). Server-only: never
# add NEXT_PUBLIC_ to them, never share them, never commit them. Leave both
# out and Buddy simply says AI is not set up.
#
# Gemini: your own key from aistudio.google.com (Get API key). The free tier
# costs nothing within Google's limits, but Google may use what is sent to
# improve its products, so use made-up messages only.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-key
#
# Claude: your own key from console.anthropic.com (Settings > API Keys). Set a
# monthly spend limit in the Anthropic Console before adding it.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-key

# --- Gmail inbox (Phase 5, optional) ---
# Lets an owner connect one Gmail inbox, read-only. Create the first two in the
# Google Cloud console (APIs & Services > Credentials > OAuth client ID, type
# "Web application", redirect URI http://localhost:3000/api/gmail/callback).
# Server-only: never add NEXT_PUBLIC_, never share them, never commit them.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
#
# GMAIL_TOKEN_KEY encrypts the Gmail sign-in before it is stored. Make your own
# with this PowerShell command and paste the output after the = sign:
#   [Convert]::ToBase64String((1..32 | ForEach-Object { Get-Random -Maximum 256 }))
# Changing it later means connecting Gmail again.
# GMAIL_TOKEN_KEY=your-generated-key
